Thought of a new item that might be fun.  I'm not in any position to
add it myself; this is just something I'd like the implementors to
consider.

Have a Wand of Hot Lead.  When you zap it in a direction, the message
should be "Bang! There is a puff of smoke" and you do 1d10 or so
damage to the target, if it's within 100' or so.  Maybe determine
whether you hit the target as you would with a range weapon.  If you
zap it at a nearby wall, the message is "Bang! Ching! You are hit!"
and you take the 1d10 damage.  There are also possible variants:

Wand of Hot Lead (rifle): Range of 300'
Wand of Hot Lead (shotgun): + for accuracy
Wand of Hot Lead (semi-auto): Message is 
	"Bang! Bang! There are two puffs of smoke." and it does twice
	the damage (and uses two charges per round).  When zapped with
	one charge, it becomes empty and doesn't work.
Wand of Hot Lead (full-auto): Message is
	"Bang! Bang! Bang! Bang!  There are many puffs of smoke."
	You have to zap it again on the next round, otherwise it keeps
	firing ^H^H^H^H^H^H^Hzapping in the same direction until you
	stop it or it runs empty.  Uses four charges per round.
	If it has 3 or fewer charges, using it fails and wastes all
	charges.  Recoil may cause stun.

and then there's the "Potion of Hot Lead" that causes death if you try
to drink it and do not immediately throw it (message is "You arm the
device and hold it to your mouth.  It contains no liquid." followed by
"There is a *LOUD* bang.  You are a puff of smoke." and a tombstone if
you don't immediately throw it), but waits a turn and does damage like
a few fireballs (but no immunity) if thrown.  (The thrower should take
damage too if within range.)

You could also have the "Potion of Anthrax" that creates a contagious
poisoning of the creatures on a level (including you!), or the useless
wand of shoulder-launched nuclear missile that kills everything,
including you, if zapped (except Morogoth teleports away!), or the
wand of Tear Gas that generates balls of confuse monster ... but this
is getting silly.
